From 907ebf4b29ed7fe9cb7531980ab21c4338cc6471 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:53:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] test(compose): check the instance check and redeploy
 metrics

The smoke already exercises both runtime paths that the new counters
describe: a fake instance exits and the periodic check reports it, and
the control plane restarts so that the startup check finds the
instance gone. Scrape the control plane's /metrics after each of them,
so a deployment built from the images shows the same counts as the
unit tests.

The first scrape checks that the counters are exported at zero. After
the lost instance, the periodic check has reported exactly one loss
and one redeployment was started (updates and deletions change the
phase before stopping an instance, so no other loss can be seen).
After the restart the counters start from zero again: the startup
check reported one loss, one redeployment was started and no
allocation was reclaimed. No periodic check may have failed.
